{"name":"Crazy","hex":"#e5cb3f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crazy","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of unsound mind; insane; demented. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Out of control."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Very, extremely."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crazy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Insanity","blocks":[{"text":"Insanity, madness, lunacy, moon-addled, and craziness are behaviors caused by certain abnormal mental or behavioral patterns. Insanity can manifest as violations of societal norms, including a person or persons becoming a danger to themselves or to other people. Conceptually, mental insanity also is associated with the biological phenomenon of contagion as in the case of copycat suicides. In contemporary usage, the term insanity is an informal, un-scientific term denoting \"mental instability\"; thus, the term insanity defense is the legal definition of mental instability. In medicine, the general term psychosis is used to include the presence of delusions or hallucinations in a patient; and psychiatric illness is \"psychopathology\", not mental insanity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/The_Rake%27s_Progress_8.jpg/330px-The_Rake%27s_Progress_8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Insanity"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Casa_de_locos.jpg/500px-Casa_de_locos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Casa_de_locos.jpg/500px-Casa_de_locos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Goya's Madhouse, 1812-1819","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACasa_de_locos.jpg"}],"sounds":{"crazy":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d6/En-us-crazy.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/d/d6/En-us-crazy.ogg/En-us-crazy.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Etymology of a Classical Meitei language term for “yellow colour”","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Etymology_of_a_Classical_Meitei_language_term_for_%E2%80%9Cyellow_colour%E2%80%9D.jpg/500px-Etymology_of_a_Classical_Meitei_language_term_for_%E2%80%9Cyellow_colour%E2%80%9D.jpg","ratio":1.3333333333333333,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Etymology_of_a_Classical_Meitei_language_term_for_%E2%80%9Cyellow_colour%E2%80%9D.jpg","share":0.561875},{"title":"Restaurant Amigos de Acapulco (window), Chico","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Restaurant_Amigos_de_Acapulco_%28window%29%2C_Chico.jpg/500px-Restaurant_Amigos_de_Acapulco_%28window%29%2C_Chico.jpg","ratio":1.5496983169260083,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Restaurant_Amigos_de_Acapulco_(window),_Chico.jpg","share":0.385},{"title":"Yellow Portulaca flower in sunshine, on black background","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Yellow_Portulaca_flower_in_sunshine%2C_on_black_background.jpg/500px-Yellow_Portulaca_flower_in_sunshine%2C_on_black_background.jpg","ratio":1,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yellow_Portulaca_flower_in_sunshine,_on_black_background.jpg","share":0.101875},{"title":"Hoverfly January 2008-6","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Hoverfly_January_2008-6.jpg/500px-Hoverfly_January_2008-6.jpg","ratio":1.250655021834061,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hoverfly_January_2008-6.jpg","share":0.09875},{"title":"Yellow Color","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Yellow_Color.jpg/500px-Yellow_Color.jpg","ratio":1.3333333333333333,"link":"https://commons.wik